VERDICT:
  The SDiff 'grieta' (anisotropic stress is not canceled) is real
  in principle, but σ_X < 2.633e-02 caps the mechanism. Even eps=1
  gives |γ−1| ~ few×10⁻² — still O(1)–O(10)× below Maus/Sakr targets.
  Observable slip requires shear DECOUPLED from the BAO-bounded
  isotropic residual (or amplification of A0). That is no longer
  this stochastic mechanism alone — it is generic anisotropic
  stress / MG (Clifton+Ferreira+Padilla+Skordis degeneracy).

